# Copy this to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values before running
# docker compose up. Lives at <deploy-root>/<environment>/deploy/.env
# on the server — read by docker-compose.yml, and by
# deploy/configure-nginx.sh (over SSH) — nowhere else, deliberately, so
# there's a single source of truth per environment (see
# deploy/configure-nginx.sh's own header for why there's no CLI
# override).

# persona's public landing page domain. Chosen 2026-09-30 (see P001's
# "Naming" section): solemn.network is the Nostr-based attestation
# protocol's own home, and this page (persona, the identity/recovery/
# trust product built on that protocol) is deployed at its apex for
# now, at the operator's explicit direction — persona.solemn.network
# remains the documented longer-term subdomain if/once a separate
# protocol-spec page is built for the apex itself.
#   live: solemn.network
#   dev:  (pick a dev-only subdomain once a dev environment is needed)
PERSONA_DOMAIN=

# ---- Second environment (dev), optional ----
#
# Running a second, fully concurrent environment on the *same* Docker
# host needs its own path — <deploy-root>/dev, alongside live's own
# <deploy-root>/live (see deploy/environments.sh) — each with its own
# deploy/.env, and in that second .env, a distinct PERSONA_DOMAIN plus
# non-colliding host ports and a Docker network subnet. Every value
# below defaults to live's own original values if left unset, so
# live's own .env needs none of this.
#
# Live's own defaults, for reference (do NOT copy this line — it's not
# what to paste, see the actual copy-paste block right below it):
#   persona-caddy: 9460 / 9200 — picked 2026-09-30 to sit past both
#   cinder's (9180-9184/9443-9447 live, 9280-9284/9543-9547 dev) and
#   EphemNet's (9190/9450 live, 9290/9550 dev) existing ranges on `bh2`.
#   Not yet verified against the real server's actual running
#   containers — do that before the first real deploy (see
#   deploy/README.md).
#
# COPY-PASTE BLOCK — uncomment and paste exactly as-is below into a
# second environment's own .env (delete the leading "# " from each
# line, change nothing else — no extra spaces, nothing added after the
# number on the same line, or configure-nginx.sh's own strict
# `grep -E '^NAME='` won't match it at all and will silently fall back
# to live's own port instead — see cinder's/EphemNet's own history for
# the real incident this comment exists to prevent):
# PERSONA_CADDY_HTTPS_PORT=9560
# PERSONA_CADDY_HTTP_PORT=9300

# Docker network subnet (must not overlap live's own — see
# deploy/docker-compose.yml's own networks: section for live's default,
# 172.31.1.0/24). Same copy-paste rule as above:
# PERSONA_EDGE_SUBNET=172.31.2.0/24
